== (B) the bounded-defect cage H0'(k0) at the p >= 700 grid ==
  caging grid: 96 primes 701..1381, sum ln = 664.6 > 657.6
  weakest 14-coprime rung: 755/10568 (l=8, p=1321); micro-gap width 1/73976 ~ 1.35e-05
  k0=0: voting classes 2, J-degeneracies 0/1, binding degree 26, H0'(0) ~ 665
  k0=1: voting classes 26, J-degeneracies 1/169, binding degree 24, H0'(1) ~ 1
  k0=2: voting classes 156, J-degeneracies 12/6084, binding degree 22, H0'(2) ~ 1
  caged conclusion at k0: 13-k0 of the speeds are EXACTLY a dilate sub-multiset of AP or GW;
  the k0 remaining speeds are free integers -- the k0-FAR STRATUM (mac-mini S125's landing zone).

== (C) the repricing conjunction statement ==
  measured shell sizes at p >= 700: 1-5 distinct greedy-reachable covers/prime (parts A, c93b);
  85-prime safe caging set budget-feasible (c93).  The sieve's I-phase collapses from the
  10^25-scale representative space to ~10^1-2 shell members per prime IFF the shell theorem
  supplies per-prime COMPLETENESS certificates (nothing improper outside the shell).
  Without completeness the exhaustive grind returns; with it the whole finite check is
  [shell verification, trivial] x [~100 primes].  The computational twin and the analytic
  descent are therefore ONE lead: the F_p counting proof IS the cost collapse.
